hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24220","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam narrated to us, a freedman of the family of Umar narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Isa ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam al-Zuraqi, from his grandmother Habibah bint Shariq: That she was with her father, when Budayl ibn Warqa' was on al-Adba', the mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), making it kneel, and he called out: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever was fasting, let him break his fast, for they are days of eating and drinking."
